  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a suru-verb ({感化|かんか}する). Most often appears in the passive form {感化|かんか}される (to be influenced). Carries a positive or neutral nuance of being changed for the better through someone's example.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- 〜に{感化|かんか}される (to be influenced by ~)\n- {感化|かんか}を{受|う}ける (to receive influence)\n- {感化|かんか}{院|いん} (reformatory — historical term)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {影響|えいきょう}: influence — more general and neutral, can be positive or negative\n- {触発|しょくはつ}: inspiration, stimulus — being spurred to action by something",
